WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.068
-Thank you so much.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.402
-Goodness, so nice to be here.
Thank you so much.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.037
-Dude, look at that.
They love you.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.572
We all love you.
How's that feel?

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:08.307
When the audience --
-It feels crazy.

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.409
I mean, this is the first time
I've been on a TV show

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:11.911
in, you know,
a year and a half or whatever.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.446
Right? In a room
with a bunch of people.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.747
-Yeah, it's bizarre.
-It's amazing.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:16.315
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:18.584
-I'm so happy too.
Thanks for having me. Thank you.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:19.952
-Every time you come on,

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.187
and thank you
for doing our show,

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.023
I mean, doing all those --
it was just crazy times.

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:27.060
You were saying of course
you were getting back to work.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.095
-Yeah, yeah.
-But everything was shut down.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.798
And you were -- you said that
you changed your laundry room

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.365
into like 10 different rooms.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:34.534
-We were -- We were in

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.201
our little tiny house
out in Long Island.

00:00:36.201 --> 00:00:37.369
-Yup.
-Just me and my husband

00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:38.638
and our teenage daughter.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.808
And we only had one little space
where we could all work,

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.076
and that was the laundry room,

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.912
and it was also where
my husband's office was,

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.080
and it was where I did yoga.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.648
It's where my daughter
did homework.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.883
That's where I recorded
an animated movie.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.352
In this laundry room.
-Wow. Did you really?

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.586
-Yeah, yeah.
And they would be like,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.255
"Do you have a space
that's a little less live?

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:57.323
A little less echoey?"

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.324
I'm like, "No."
-No.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.558
-"This is it."

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:01.995
-Everyone found a new room
during this whole thing.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.830
-We'd stick towels under
the door. Yeah, this is it.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.799
And we'd rotate in and out of
there, 'cause yeah, you know.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.101
-Wait. Is this spirit?
Is that --

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:10.369
-"Spirit Untamed."
Yeah.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:11.403
-"Spirit Untamed."
I've read about this.

00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:12.672
-Your daughters will love this.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.073
-My kids are into "Spirit."
They love "Spirit."

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.107
-Yeah, they love horses
and all that.

00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:16.209
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.244
-Next Friday,
your new series,

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.013
"Lisey's Story," comes out.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.081
-This is Stephen King.
-Stephen King, yeah.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:25.451
-This is not your first foray
into scary.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:29.155
-No. It's not my first
scary-movie event.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:32.191
-No, your first scary movie
was -- Everyone remembers.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:33.726
-Oh, sure.
You'll remember this one.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.494
-"Tales From the Dark Side,"
the movie.

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:37.763
Look at you there.
-Yeah. That's me. That's me.

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:38.998
-Now that is you
somewhere under there?

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.332
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:40.332 --> 00:01:41.534
-And what do you remember
about this?

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.936
-Well, you know what's
interesting about this

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.404
is that this is the part
of the movie --

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.672
I really remember this because
this is a part of the movie

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.140
that I didn't think
that I was in.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.444
It was my first movie,
this horror movie,

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.511
and we were shooting it
in Yonkers.

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:54.581
I was so excited
to get this horror movie.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:55.447
-Yeah.

00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:56.982
-And I have a tendency even now

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:58.451
not to read anything
but the dialogue,

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.852
you know, when I get a script.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.353
Because I don't like
stage directions.

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:02.989
I don't like hearing, you know,

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.857
"She walks down the street
jauntily."

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:06.125
I know
I'll walk down the street.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.126
I might not be jaunty.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.561
I don't want to know
what they think.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:09.862
-Yeah, you're acting.
-I'm gonna figure it out.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.298
Right? So I don't read
any of the stage directions.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.168
So on this job,
it was a really quick job,

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.403
I finished, and I got killed
by the mummy,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.272
and I went over to the director
to say good-bye

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:21.940
and thank you for this
great opportunity.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.576
And he was like,
"You're not done."

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.677
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.112
I'm like "No,
this is my last scene."

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.313
He goes, "No, no.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.482
You didn't finish reading
the script, did you?"

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.585
Because -- Because I turn
into a mummy at the end.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:33.752
-Yeah, come back.

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:35.521
-And I come back
and I kill somebody else.

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.223
But it was all
in stage directions,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.457
and I never read it.

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:41.093
So it was so incredibly
unprofessional of me.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:42.762
-But look at you --
-I didn't read the script.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.798
-Yeah, but look at you now.
It's all worked out.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.600
I lost my voice
earlier in the week.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.835
-It sounds good.
Sounds sexy.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:52.104
-It is sexy, right?
-Yeah. Sexy voice.

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:53.305
-Thank you.
Please tell my wife that.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:54.941
-Sexy Fallon.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.809
What would that be like,
sexy Fallon?

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.644
But you've screamed before.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.346
Do you have any tips?

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.882
-You can't scream
without losing your voice.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.150
-You just can't?
-I would have to --

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.953
The director of "Lisey's Story"
would always --

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.755
I would say, "Please save
the screaming

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.323
that you want me to do
until Friday night,

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.958
because I'm going to need
two days to recover,"

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:14.526
because I'd always blow out
my voice,

00:03:14.526 --> 00:03:16.262
and I wanted it to be better
on a Monday.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.964
But then, like --
so every Friday,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:21.100
he'd be like, "You ready?
We're gonna do some screaming."

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.102
But this one weekend,
I had an audition

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.803
for "Dear Evan Hansen"
the next day.

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:25.805
So he was like --
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.740
Yeah.
So he was like, "Scream."

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.975
And I'm like,
"I don't want to scream."

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:33.079
He's like, "Scream."
And I was like, aaaaah.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.148
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:39.052
-"That's your scream?"
Aaaah.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:43.022
-I was like...
♪ I have an audition ♪

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.857
♪ I can't blow out my voice ♪

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.792
-Yeah.
How'd the audition go?

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:49.929
-I mean, you know, hopefully
it didn't sound like that.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.230
-Yeah.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.465
-I did get the job.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.533
-You got the part. Yeah.
-I got the job.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.734
So that was great.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.035
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I saw the trailer.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.236
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:58.504
-The trailer came out --

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.473
-Such a good trailer, right?
-Oh, dude, that guy.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.241
-And Ben Platt is a genius.
-Ben Platt is insane.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:03.676
"Lisey's Story."
-Yeah.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:07.579
-This is based on a Stephen King
book, very popular.

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.715
How do we describe it?

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:13.252
-Okay. So Lisey is a woman
who's married to a famous writer

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.321
who has -- at the beginning of
the story,

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.089
you realize he's been dead
for a couple of years.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:19.859
And so she's kind of
living her life by herself,

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:23.662
but she's getting all these
weird messages from her past.

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:24.997
At the same time,
this other guy,

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:27.700
one of her husband's fans --
he's a horror writer --

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.402
is stalking her.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:32.505
So it's kind of
a really complicated

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:36.342
psychological horror drama.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.344
It's good.
-Of course it is. Yeah.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.580
It's on Apple TV Plus.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.915
Here's Julianne Moore
in "Lisey's Story."

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.050
Take a look.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.619
-Funny that you --
that you came today

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.553
'cause I was just looking
at your picture

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.921
in the Horlick's yearbook.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:52.391
Picture of the hero who saves
a famous writer's life,

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:55.394
but, um, I think reality,
you ran like a rabbit.

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:56.995
-Mrs. Landon.
-You came back, though,

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:58.597
to get your picture taken
and to grab the credit.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:00.365
I mean, I don't care about that.
I never cared about credit.

00:05:00.365 --> 00:05:01.667
I don't care about that at all,

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.202
but you are not
getting in there,

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.071
and you are never
going to see his papers.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:07.606
-You were nothing but
a restaurant hostess

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:09.175
when you caught his eye.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.110
The fact
that you slept in his bed

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.047
does not give you the right to
withhold his unwritten papers

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:15.681
from the rest of the world.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.617
-Oh, my God.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.385
-Julianne Moore, everybody!

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.920
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.189
-I think I just --
-Spit everywhere.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:27.259
-"Lisey's Story" premieres
Friday, June 4th

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:28.728
on Apple TV Plus.

